    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003ePork loin is the cheap cut that works here because it is sliced thin.\u003c/strong\u003e Thin slices cook in seconds and never get the chance to dry out, which is why you do not need to pay up for tenderloin.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eFirm the loin in the freezer for half an hour before slicing.\u003c/strong\u003e That one step lets a regular kitchen knife cut it as thin as the pre-sliced hot pot packs that cost twice as much.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eFresh ginger is the entire identity of this dish.\u003c/strong\u003e Buy a big knob, grate what you need, and freeze the rest. Powder will not get you there.",
